WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.040
Sure are leaving us hanging, huh?

3
00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:46.410
Is there a way to repair it?

4
00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:52.830
<b>Creeping Future</b>

5
00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:48.480
Shh! Sounds like it's clearing up!

6
00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.510
The Whitebeard Pirates were defeated?

7
00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:52.950
That means the good guys won, right?

8
00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:58.550
Repeat, this is Navy headquarters with
an update regarding the battle at Marineford.

9
00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:03.050
Although Whitebeard and his allies made
the conflict a long and arduous affair,

10
00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:06.220
the Marines struggled valiantly
in the name of justice.

11
00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:10.230
We are pleased to report that our
victory over Whitebeard was absolute,

12
00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:13.170
and the execution of
Portgas D. Ace was carried out.

13
00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.940
You are once again safe
from the treachery of pirates

14
00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:18.500
thanks to the Navy and
World Government's efforts!

15
00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:22.840
We did it!

16
00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:30.150
We're invincible! No one can
match the power of the Navy!

17
00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:40.990
Just you wait, someday they'll summon
me to serve at HQ, and I'll be ready!

18
00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.330
Thank goodness, the war's finally over!

19
00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:47.840
All right!

20
00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.550
I thought it'd never end!

21
00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:53.060
Whitebeard's reign of terror
is over! Party time!

22
00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.600
The good guys beat
the bad ones, right, Mom?

23
00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:02.060
That's right, and we
have the Navy to thank!

24
00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.270
I knew they could do it!

25
00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:04.470
Take that, pirates!

26
00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.240
I thought we were goners!

27
00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.660
- Now, three cheers!
- Yeah!

28
00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.030
- one for the admirals,
- Yeah!

29
00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.340
and a big one for all the Marines!

30
00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:28.670
Back at Marineford and far away from
celebrations of the Navy victory,

31
00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:30.970
there are seven ships afloat.

32
00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:34.090
Those who will soon take
part in the new pirate era

33
00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:37.610
are witnessing one of the
great turning points in history.

34
00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.650
Ever mindful of the Navy's
ruthless sense of justice,

35
00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:45.840
they still stare upon the aftermath
of war, knowing the ensuing chaos will

36
00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:50.830
leave plenty of opportunity
for new powers to arise.

37
00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:52.580
Captain Drake, sir.

38
00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:55.690
At last the war's over.

39
00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:59.930
Both sides are weakened,
Navy and the pirates...

40
00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:01.920
It's just a matter of time.

41
00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:06.030
Whitebeard's territory... Other
pirates will be vyin' for control.

42
00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:07.960
It's bound to get pretty rough.

43
00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:11.070
Now Blackbeard's reign has begun.

44
00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:15.640
Not only has he built a formidable crew,
but he's got two Devil Fruit powers.

45
00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.530
Just our luck. It's gonna be a while

46
00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:20.670
before we've got the strength
to topple those guys!

47
00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:26.020
It's all his fault.

48
00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:30.830
Damn that Blackbeard!
I'll find him and make him pay!

49
00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.670
All right! Let's go!

50
00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:35.100
Yeah!

51
00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.200
What the hell is going on?

52
00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.140
What are you talkin' about,
cap'n? Is somethin' wrong?

53
00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:42.580
Trafalgar Law is
no friend of Straw Hat.

54
00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:45.000
Why is he saving him now?
What's the catch?

55
00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:45.860
Huh?

56
00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:48.060
Law has got a reputation.

57
00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:51.310
He's one of the North Blue's
most brutal pirates.

58
00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:56.780
There's no way he'd've saved him unless
he was expecting something back in return.

59
00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.590
How odd.

60
00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.990
Captain Hawkins, what
seems to be the matter?

61
00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:06.590
I've been trying to determine if

62
00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:11.700
Straw Hat Luffy is alive or
dead, but the cards won't say.

63
00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:18.160
To tell you the truth, this war
had me pretty worked up at first.

64
00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:21.150
Never thought the great
Whitebeard would die.

65
00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:23.790
Well, either way, it's over.

66
00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:25.360
Yeah, guess so.

67
00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:35.080
Nothing's ever over!

68
00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:40.030
One old bastard kicks the bucket and
an even meaner one takes his place.

69
00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:42.470
Blackbeard's gonna turn
everything upside down.

70
00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:49.470
See, before, the Four
Emperors ran the New World.

71
00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:53.870
Whitebeard, Kaido, Big Mom, and Shanks.

72
00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:57.480
But now that Whitebeard is dead,
everything is out of balance

73
00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.910
and no one knows how
the scales are gonna tip.

74
00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:04.920
It's a brand new era, like none before,
and it's ours for the taking!

75
00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:19.480
News of the Navy's victory
in the war at Marineford,

76
00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:24.590
the deadliest battle since the dawn of the
Great Pirate Era, spread like wildfire,

77
00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:28.920
and people across the world
are celebrating the good news.

78
00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:31.630
<b>East Blue</b>

79
00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:30.360
The East Blue.

80
00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:31.860
All right!

81
00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:34.230
Whitebeard is dead at last!

82
00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:35.630
Good riddance!

83
00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:37.400
You said it!

84
00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.640
What a relief!

85
00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:41.910
<b>West Blue</b>

86
00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.100
The West Blue.

87
00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:44.520
We can finally sail in peace!

88
00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.060
Raise your glasses!

89
00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:49.250
<b>South Blue</b>

90
00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:48.160
The South Blue.

91
00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.930
Celebratory sale over here!

92
00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:52.570
Over here, too! Get your party food!

93
00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:57.960
<b>North Blue</b>

94
00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.330
The North Blue.

95
00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:01.080
Oh, man!
That really hit the spot!

96
00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.420
Keep the drinks coming!

97
00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.380
Next round is on the house!

98
00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:07.900
<b>Grand Line</b>

99
00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:06.980
The Grand Line.

100
00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:08.910
Can we join the Navy, too?

101
00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:10.580
I'm gonna beat all the pirates!

102
00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:12.080
Nuh-uh! I am!

103
00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:14.680
Yeah, right!

104
00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:18.020
Thank you, and may this peace last!

105
00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:23.460
As it goes with history,
the passage of time distorts facts

106
00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.960
and glosses over important details.

107
00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:30.380
Soon, the only two words that
stand out are "Navy victory."

108
00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:35.590
Lost in the celebration, most people failed
to consider the war's real consequences.

109
00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:37.990
What was that?

110
00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:43.160
You're all fools!

111
00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.430
Didn't you hear him?

112
00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:47.300
The One Piece...
Whitebeard said it's real!

113
00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:49.930
So, Gold Roger wasn't lying after all!

114
00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:52.300
Well, guess we better
get to finding it!

115
00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:54.500
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

116
00:08:56.130 --> 00:09:00.500
Enough wasting away in
this dump! Time to set sail!

117
00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:04.370
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

118
00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:08.840
Though "Navy victory"
might have a nice ring to it,

119
00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:10.600
<b>New World - Foodvalten</b>

120
00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:12.580
it does not necessarily
equate to peace.

121
00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:19.950
You guys aren't welcome here!

122
00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:22.350
Get out of our town!

123
00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:28.090
For Whitebeard was a pirate,
but he was also a protector,

124
00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:32.870
and news of his death emboldened
pirates who previously cowered from him.

125
00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:37.160
Don't worry.

126
00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:40.600
I've turned all the Marines
onboard into stone.

127
00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:43.670
So, what is Luffy's condition?
Will he be all right?

128
00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:47.100
Can I help somehow? Anything at all.

129
00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:50.220
Gosh, I was afraid the Navy
was still hot on our tail,

130
00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:52.280
but I don't understand.
How did you know the sub

131
00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:54.580
was gonna surface right here and now?

132
00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:56.880
I simply had Salome track
your ship underwater.

133
00:09:58.050 --> 00:09:59.720
- Oh.
- Don't change the subject,

134
00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:02.320
Luffy is all that matters!

135
00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:03.190
You're right.

136
00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:04.160
– Really, dude?!
– Really, dude?!

137
00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:06.890
Oh, Captain!

138
00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:10.720
<b>Captain Trafalgar Law
Heart Pirates</b>

139
00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:10.860
I did everything I possibly could.

140
00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:13.660
So, does that mean...
that he'll be okay?

141
00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.360
We'll just have to wait and see.

142
00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:18.710
He's in stable condition
for now. However...

143
00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:23.060
He took on a lot more damage
than most could endure,

144
00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:25.700
and there's no guarantee
that he'll survive.

145
00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:31.440
What an uplifting prognosis!

146
00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:32.400
Who said that?

147
00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:34.100
Me, duh!

148
00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:38.040
Anyhow, if you want Straw Boy to wake up,
you're gonna have to show him some love!

149
00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:40.480
We owe him our lives,
so take good care of him!

150
00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:42.810
We'd still be in prison
without his help!

151
00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:46.040
Now, all the Newkama can finally
go to the Kamabakka Kingdom,

152
00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.440
like we've always dreamed!

153
00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:48.640
Off we go!

154
00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:51.910
Farewell, Straw Hat,
we're heading home!

155
00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:57.430
So, uh, who are they?

156
00:10:57.430 --> 00:11:00.030
They are a group of
prisoners from Impel Down.

157
00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:02.000
It appears that Luffy is their friend.

158
00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.140
They must have snuck
onto the ship as well.

159
00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:09.480
I can't believe he pushed his
body past its limit a second time!

160
00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:13.330
That's how strong the bond was
between Straw Boy and Ace Boy!

161
00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:14.500
You tell 'em, Iva!

162
00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:18.450
Nothing could stop him then and
nothing will stop him now, right?

163
00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:23.420
I wish that were so,
but fate can be cruel.

164
00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:26.030
You can't save everyone.

165
00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:29.700
All of that work for nothing!

166
00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:32.710
He's nearly dead because that's
the kind of world this is!

167
00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:34.040
Don't get down now, Iva!

168
00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:36.310
Straw Hat can pull
through this, I know it!

169
00:11:36.310 --> 00:11:39.820
Ya gotta live, Straw Hat!
Don't you dare die on us!

170
00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:48.110
Luffy has touched so many lives!

171
00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:53.050
If only there was some way I could
take his place so that he may survive!

172
00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:56.220
Poor darling!

173
00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:58.920
So lucky.

174
00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:01.950
Must be nice having the Pirate
Empress fawn over you like that.

175
00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.090
Yeah, wow.

176
00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:04.400
You're a new face.

177
00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:06.380
Are you one of Straw Boy's pals?

178
00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:10.790
No. I can't say why I saved him,
or it's complicated at least.

179
00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.820
Are you gonna pressure
me for the details?

180
00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:16.850
No, no. Let's just say that your
heart guided you to his side.

181
00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:17.960
Hey, wait!

182
00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:19.420
You can't walk around yet!

183
00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.330
Don't push your body like that!

184
00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:23.460
Captain told you to rest, remember?

185
00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:25.100
Your wound could open up!

186
00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:27.100
Come back here, please!

187
00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:30.470
Leave me be.

188
00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:33.370
Jimbei...

189
00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:37.210
I know you...

190
00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:39.740
Captain Law from the North Blue.

191
00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.370
Hm.

192
00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:45.710
You look awful, should you really
be moving around like that?

193
00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:48.510
I owe you...

194
00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:51.830
I owe you my life!

195
00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.980
Enough. Lie down.

196
00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:57.020
My mind is troubled.

197
00:12:57.020 --> 00:13:01.050
Luffy...the pain I feel for him
is such that I can't rest.

198
00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:02.820
I have failed you, friend.

199
00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:04.100
Remorse...

200
00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:08.140
If this is how I feel,
then just imagine him.

201
00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:09.970
His collapse may have been a mercy,

202
00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:14.140
since it allowed us to take
him away, but what now?

203
00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:17.910
Even if he survives,
with the immensity of his loss,

204
00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:20.910
I fear for the moment he awakens.

205
00:13:27.690 --> 00:13:29.060
You, the fuzzy one.

206
00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:30.860
Where's your transponder snail?

207
00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:33.280
Who, me?

208
00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:36.150
Uh, I'll go get it! If you'd like...

209
00:13:36.150 --> 00:13:39.420
No fair. I wish I got to
serve the empress, too!

210
00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.000
Mmm-hmm.

211
00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.400
I will summon the Kuja ship,

212
00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:46.020
so we can sail across the Calm
Belt, even with this submarine.

213
00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:50.460
The World Government can't find out Luffy's
alive, or else they'll come after him!

214
00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:52.930
Let us harbor him safely
at the Maiden Island!

215
00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:56.000
Really?

216
00:13:56.000 --> 00:14:01.070
As long as they still view me as a Warlord,
Luffy will not be in danger there!

217
00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:22.330
Fleet Admiral Sengoku!

218
00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:26.700
I'm very sorry for the intrusion, sir,

219
00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:29.100
but we've just received
urgent news from Impel Down!

220
00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:30.340
Should I continue, sir?

221
00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:32.640
Magellan, is he all right?

222
00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:35.340
He was beaten
badly and is barely alive.

223
00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:40.440
The medical team has been working on his
injuries nonstop, but Magellan is ashamed

224
00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:43.280
and he's blaming himself
for what happened down there.

225
00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:47.470
If his wounds weren't so severe, then he'd
probably be at risk of killing himself.

226
00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:50.450
Don't tell me that nonsense!
He knows how much we need him!

227
00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:52.690
Uhh, yes, sir! Of course.

228
00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:56.790
What exactly did happen at Impel Down?

229
00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:58.960
Things there are quite disastrous.

230
00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:04.460
The situation on Level 6 is
especially dire. It's a crisis.

231
00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.980
Elaborate.

232
00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:12.010
<b>Impel Down, the Undersea Prison</b>

233
00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:15.230
What's wrong, boys?

234
00:15:15.230 --> 00:15:20.800
Feelin' a bit down, thinkin' you'll
be stuck in this hellhole forever?

235
00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:23.200
Just waitin' till ya die, huh?

236
00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:26.020
So, how about this? Start fighting.

237
00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:28.490
Start fighting right there,
in your jail cells!

238
00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:30.090
Huh?

239
00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:33.960
Those of you who survive get
a free ticket to join my crew

240
00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:35.560
and sail outta here with me!

241
00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:36.860
Is he for real?

242
00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:38.260
It's time to play!

243
00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:40.360
Now, who should I kill first?

244
00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:52.380
He had his pick of the
deadliest criminals in the world

245
00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:55.780
and he had them fight to the death,
while he simply stood there and watched?

246
00:15:55.780 --> 00:16:01.020
Yes, but only four of the prisoners were
taken... San Juan Wolf, Avalo Pizarro,

247
00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:04.230
Vasco Shot, and
Catarina Devon, as you saw.

248
00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:08.130
But I'm sorry to say, sir, that his
new recruits aren't the only prisoners

249
00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:10.300
who are missing from Level 6.

250
00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:12.400
I...

251
00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:22.830
So, Impel Down is
swimming with escaped criminals,

252
00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.490
the worst the world has ever seen.

253
00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:28.030
We can't let a single
one of them get away.

254
00:16:28.030 --> 00:16:31.270
If they stole a ship and slipped
into some country unnoticed,

255
00:16:31.270 --> 00:16:34.440
there's no telling what sort
of terrible things might happen!

256
00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:37.710
Start a count of how many
Level 6 prisoners are missing.

257
00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:41.250
Get their names and put out a most
wanted list as soon as possible.

258
00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:44.820
What's wrong?

259
00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:47.950
Well, uh, actually...

260
00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:50.420
I'm under direct orders
from the World Government

261
00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:53.120
to keep this matter
a secret at any cost.

262
00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:53.860
Huh?

263
00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:58.660
A huge blunder like this one could
badly hurt the government's reputation.

264
00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:05.070
I don't give a damn!

265
00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:36.890
Doflamingo! You bastard!

266
00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:40.200
Come on! Lighten up!

267
00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:42.830
We both know you're
too weak to be a Warlord!

268
00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:43.530
Just face it!

269
00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:47.340
I'll do you a favor
for old time's sake.

270
00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:49.540
We won't say the government
had you put down,

271
00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:52.510
we'll say you gave your life in battle.

272
00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:56.250
So, Sengoku put you up to this?
I'll tear him apart!

273
00:17:57.010 --> 00:18:00.840
Nah, think higher up the ladder.

274
00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:06.990
<b>West Blue</b>

275
00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:25.470
A pirate ship is approaching
Lascamp in the West Blue!

276
00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:27.870
But we don't have any
forces nearby that can help!

277
00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.240
Contact the closest base!

278
00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:33.650
Reinforcements from the 80th
division are on their way!

279
00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:36.700
This is the South Blue!

280
00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:38.810
Currently checking
the location of the attack!

281
00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:39.850
Damn it!

282
00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:41.680
The pirates are supposed
to be afraid of us!

283
00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.520
Headquarters dealt them
a major blow at Marineford,

284
00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:46.330
not to mention Whitebeard
is dead, so what gives?

285
00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:48.320
You would've thought they'd
be laying low after the war,

286
00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:50.250
but they're running wild everywhere!

287
00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:52.860
I wonder what's gotten into those guys?

288
00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:55.140
Pirates have started raiding Lascamp!

289
00:18:55.140 --> 00:18:57.110
Communication has also been lost!

290
00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:58.410
Proceed to send backup!

291
00:18:58.410 --> 00:18:59.210
I repeat!

292
00:18:59.210 --> 00:19:01.050
Send backup now!

293
00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:04.660
All right boys, load her up!

294
00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:07.130
After that it's on to the Grand Line!

295
00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:16.650
<b>New World - Foodvalten</b>

296
00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:16.490
Two weeks after the War of the Best
concluded, the world began to witness

297
00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:19.400
the consequences
of Whitebeard's defeat.

298
00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:25.830
You guys aren't welcome here!

299
00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:28.500
Get out of our town!

300
00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:34.370
You didn't hear the news?

301
00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:43.240
Then lemme tell you, this dump's been
up for grabs since Whitebeard croaked.

302
00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.610
This stupid flag
don't mean a thing now!

303
00:19:46.510 --> 00:19:47.480
That's right.

304
00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:50.120
There's no one to protect you now!

305
00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:06.020
Huh?

306
00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:08.720
Hey, twerp!

307
00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:11.730
Listen up, cause I'm only
gonna say this once.

308
00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.230
This island's under my control now!

309
00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:17.460
The name's Brownbeard
and don't you forget it!

310
00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:25.070
The war ended with the death
of Whitebeard and a Navy victory.

311
00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:27.880
Yet the peace that the World
Government hoped to achieve

312
00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:32.980
slipped through their fingers and the world
was only plunged into further unrest.

313
00:20:35.280 --> 00:20:38.790
Meanwhile, aboard the
Kuja ship Boa Hancock, Jimbei,

314
00:20:38.790 --> 00:20:42.390
and the Heart pirates make
their way toward Amazon Lily

315
00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:45.220
where they will shelter
the unconscious Luffy.

316
00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:49.570
Now then.

317
00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:54.040
This chapter of Straw Boy's life,
costarring yours truly, has come to a close.

318
00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:55.540
Heehaw!

319
00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:59.520
Jimbei, I hope you don't mind
watching over our friend in my place.

320
00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:00.450
Of course.

321
00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:03.790
My body is still too weak to swim,
but the least that I can do

322
00:21:03.790 --> 00:21:07.160
is watch over Luffy until he recovers.

323
00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:11.990
Though, I fear there is precious
little aid I can give him.

324
00:21:11.990 --> 00:21:15.000
It was a curious twist of
fate to meet you, fishman.

325
00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:15.900
Likewise.

326
00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:19.200
Although we were both imprisoned
in the lowest levels of Impel Down,

327
00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:21.640
our paths nearly didn't cross.

328
00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:24.310
Luffy carried us away
like a tidal wave.

329
00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:28.620
Though I must admit, I know not
the direction that these seas flow.

330
00:21:29.170 --> 00:21:30.720
Tidal wave is right.

331
00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:35.890
His antics at Marineford were
too turbulent even for us.

332
00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:39.990
I hate to say goodbye, my friend,
but the candy boys and girls of my kingdom

333
00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:43.130
can only wait on
their master for so long!

334
00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:45.400
Do take good care of Straw Boy for me!

335
00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:47.070
I shall miss him!

336
00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:54.610
So long! Bye! Thanks
for everything, Straw Hat!

337
00:21:54.610 --> 00:21:58.540
We'll tell tales of you in
Kamabakka Kingdom for years to come!

338
00:21:58.540 --> 00:22:01.110
When he wakes up,
be sure to say "hi" for us!

339
00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:02.850
Get well soon, Straw Boy!

340
00:22:02.850 --> 00:22:04.420
We can't wait to see you again!

341
00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:05.620
Hang in there!

342
00:22:05.620 --> 00:22:08.820
Everything's gonna be okay!

343
00:22:08.820 --> 00:22:10.910
Let's go, my darlings!

344
00:22:10.910 --> 00:22:13.580
Yeah! Off to the New Kama paradise!

345
00:22:13.580 --> 00:22:15.820
Keep leading the way, Queen Iva!

346
00:22:15.820 --> 00:22:16.620
Yessir!

347
00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:19.590
Peachy Island, here we come!

348
00:22:19.590 --> 00:22:23.460
I hate to ruin the moment, but we
really should be on our way now.

349
00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:27.290
Two weeks have passed.

350
00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:30.760
Law and his crew are staying
in the bay, continuing to treat

351
00:22:30.760 --> 00:22:33.560
Luffy's injuries without
encroaching on the island.

352
00:22:50.260 --> 00:22:53.260
What will happen to him
if he remains in that state?

353
00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:54.360
Simple.

354
00:22:54.360 --> 00:22:59.000
If he keeps flailing around,
the more likely he is to open his wound,

355
00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:02.100
and if that happens,
chances are he'll die.

356
00:23:05.370 --> 00:23:07.470
Quick! Now's our chance!

357
00:23:07.470 --> 00:23:09.010
Damn it, get off me!

358
00:23:09.010 --> 00:23:10.890
Just hold still!

359
00:23:10.890 --> 00:23:11.590
Shut up!

360
00:23:11.590 --> 00:23:12.490
Let me go!

361
00:23:15.190 --> 00:23:17.560
Where did they take you?

362
00:23:17.560 --> 00:23:19.930
Where'd you go?

363
00:23:19.930 --> 00:23:22.200
He's gone completely mad!

364
00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:23.530
Oh, Luffy.

365
00:23:23.530 --> 00:23:26.230
We've got to tell the Snake Princess!

366
00:23:26.230 --> 00:23:27.100
Princess!

367
00:23:27.100 --> 00:23:28.560
We have big news!

368
00:23:28.560 --> 00:23:30.230
Are you there?

369
00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:32.830
Luffy has finally woken up!

370
00:23:32.830 --> 00:23:33.930
Luffy is awake?

371
00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:34.670
Are you sure?

372
00:23:34.670 --> 00:23:36.140
Oh, thank goodness.

373
00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:38.500
I must rush to his side immediately.

374
00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:40.500
You cannyot!

375
00:23:40.500 --> 00:23:43.170
The kingdom is obsessed
with seeing those men.

376
00:23:43.170 --> 00:23:48.240
How can you expect them to follow our laws
if you so readily break them yourself?

377
00:23:48.240 --> 00:23:51.020
Men are prohibited in our land.

378
00:23:51.020 --> 00:23:56.200
Luffy is one thing, but I cringe at how
easily we let these strangers into the bay!

379
00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:59.270
Must you keep bending the rules?

380
00:23:59.270 --> 00:24:01.040
Yes, I know, but he needs help.

381
00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:03.590
Before worrying about that,
you should eat something.

382
00:24:03.590 --> 00:24:04.800
Your sister's right!

383
00:24:04.800 --> 00:24:08.540
Since you returned to Amazon Lily,
you've barely eaten a bite!

384
00:24:08.540 --> 00:24:09.570
Food! Yes!

385
00:24:09.570 --> 00:24:11.740
Luffy must be starving
after his recovery!

386
00:24:11.740 --> 00:24:12.900
He will need his strength!

387
00:24:12.900 --> 00:24:15.440
Go prepare a mountain
of dishes rich in nutrients!

388
00:24:15.440 --> 00:24:17.070
Yes! As you wish!

389
00:24:17.070 --> 00:24:18.770
And I shall aid you, myself.

390
00:24:18.770 --> 00:24:20.220
Onward to the kitchen!

391
00:24:20.220 --> 00:24:21.390
For Luffy!

392
00:24:23.330 --> 00:24:25.230
I can let this one pass.

393
00:24:25.230 --> 00:24:27.400
So she wants to do some cooking.

394
00:24:27.400 --> 00:24:28.770
Nyo harm in that.

395
00:24:28.770 --> 00:24:31.570
When we're done, I'll serve him myself!

396
00:24:31.570 --> 00:24:33.670
Are you even listening?

397
00:24:33.670 --> 00:24:38.380
When he gets well, we'll invite
Luffy to these chambers alone.

398
00:24:40.590 --> 00:24:41.760
What nonsense!

399
00:24:41.760 --> 00:24:42.860
I am an empress!

400
00:24:42.860 --> 00:24:44.290
You can't tell me what to do!

401
00:24:44.290 --> 00:24:45.630
Nyo means nyo!

402
00:24:45.630 --> 00:24:49.430
The well being of this country
does not revolve around you!

403
00:24:49.430 --> 00:24:50.780
You poor girl!

404
00:24:50.780 --> 00:24:54.190
You've been stricken by the
most vile illness imaginable.

405
00:24:54.190 --> 00:24:58.930
To think that our fearsome pirate
empress is lovesick, of all things!

406
00:24:58.930 --> 00:25:03.460
Luffy must have gone through hell
and back surviving both Impel Down

407
00:25:03.460 --> 00:25:06.830
and the terrible things that
happened at Navy Headquarters.

408
00:25:06.830 --> 00:25:09.800
Despite my protests,
the fact that he made it back

409
00:25:09.800 --> 00:25:13.010
here alive is nyothing
short of a miracle.

410
00:25:13.010 --> 00:25:17.210
I can't help but wonder
what the gods expect of him.

411
00:25:18.380 --> 00:25:19.810
Yo pass me the wrench.

412
00:25:19.810 --> 00:25:21.730
'Kay, here ya go.

413
00:25:21.730 --> 00:25:24.600
Hey! How're the ship
repairs coming along?

414
00:25:24.600 --> 00:25:26.340
We'll manage don't you worry.

415
00:25:26.340 --> 00:25:28.580
The rest of you ever figure out
where Straw Hat went?

416
00:25:28.580 --> 00:25:30.490
Jimbei's been gone
for a while now, too.

417
00:25:30.490 --> 00:25:33.860
Nope. Ain't got a clue.

418
00:25:33.860 --> 00:25:36.890
Someone told me that
if a man enters Amazon Lily,

419
00:25:36.890 --> 00:25:39.390
he'll be turned to
stone right on the spot.

420
00:25:39.390 --> 00:25:41.830
I'm starting to think it's
worth dying for, though.

421
00:25:41.830 --> 00:25:44.860
According to Aphelandra,
there're tons of girls.

422
00:25:44.860 --> 00:25:47.360
Way more than what we saw at the port.

423
00:25:47.360 --> 00:25:49.140
This is a one time chance.

424
00:25:49.140 --> 00:25:52.170
If I don't peek, I might regret
it for the rest of my life!

425
00:25:52.170 --> 00:25:54.310
I guess we'll both
be statues, then, huh?

426
00:25:54.310 --> 00:25:56.430
Do you think they've got girl bears?

427
00:25:56.430 --> 00:25:58.200
You're ruining our fantasy!

428
00:25:58.200 --> 00:25:59.500
Sorry I asked.

429
00:25:59.500 --> 00:26:01.340
Amazon women are humans!

430
00:26:01.340 --> 00:26:02.640
No bears for you!

431
00:26:02.640 --> 00:26:04.410
Life is cruel!

432
00:26:40.660 --> 00:26:42.060
What is this place?

433
00:26:42.060 --> 00:26:45.200
Where am I?

434
00:26:45.200 --> 00:26:46.570
Maybe.

435
00:26:46.570 --> 00:26:48.700
I dreamt the whole thing.

436
00:27:03.150 --> 00:27:05.350
Sorry, Luffy.

437
00:27:05.350 --> 00:27:06.720
I tried.

438
00:27:11.290 --> 00:27:14.930
Looks like this is as far as I can go.

439
00:27:24.270 --> 00:27:25.570
It's not true!

440
00:27:25.570 --> 00:27:27.490
It can't be!

441
00:27:27.490 --> 00:27:28.860
Luffy!

442
00:27:30.130 --> 00:27:33.000
Go away!

443
00:27:39.720 --> 00:27:40.780
Stop it!

444
00:27:40.780 --> 00:27:43.350
It's not true!

445
00:28:21.320 --> 00:28:22.380
Jimbei.

446
00:28:22.380 --> 00:28:25.450
I know I might not
make it out of this alive.

447
00:28:25.450 --> 00:28:29.760
I'm sorry, but if I die, would
you look after my brother for me?

448
00:28:32.260 --> 00:28:35.000
You must listen to me, Luffy!

449
00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:36.700
Your brother Ace is...

450
00:28:36.700 --> 00:28:37.830
Don't say it!

451
00:28:37.830 --> 00:28:40.370
Don't say anything!

452
00:28:41.170 --> 00:28:43.540
You think I don't know?

453
00:28:43.540 --> 00:28:46.750
You think I think this is a dream?

454
00:28:47.580 --> 00:28:53.950
If it were a dream,
I'd already be awake!

455
00:28:53.950 --> 00:28:56.990
But it's not, is it?

456
00:29:04.890 --> 00:29:08.460
My brother Ace is
really dead, isn't he?

457
00:29:15.600 --> 00:29:18.330
Yes, I'm afraid that he is.

458
00:29:26.430 --> 00:29:27.730
Hey, Grandpa!

459
00:29:27.730 --> 00:29:29.770
Who's this Ace fella?

460
00:29:29.770 --> 00:29:33.140
Well, funny you should ask...

461
00:29:33.140 --> 00:29:36.310
'cause Ace is gonna
be your new big brother!

462
00:29:38.240 --> 00:29:43.380
Luffy, when next we meet,
we'll both be top pirates!

463
00:29:43.380 --> 00:29:44.320
The top.

464
00:29:44.320 --> 00:29:45.660
You and me!
